{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.CrossingAdditiveWrithe","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Kronecker","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.trace_deltaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.trace_deltaS","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/DeterminantChern.lean#L111-L118","doc":"The short `Q_β` element `Δ_S = (h²/2)·1 − (h/2)(σ₁ + σ₂)` has trace\n`−(h/2)(2z − h)` under any trace with `tr(1) = 1`, `tr(σᵢ) = z`. So the ratio of\nits traces at two Markov parameters is the ratio of `(2z − h)`; between `z_D`\nand the augmentation `z = q` that ratio is `(2z_D − h)/[2]`, the Markov\naverage of `c₁` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.markov_average_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.markov_average_c1","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/DeterminantChern.lean#L91-L109","doc":"**The Markov average of `c₁`.** Let a trace decompose as `Σ_k y_k χ_k` with\n`Σ_k y_k f_k = tr(1) = 1` and `Σ_k y_k χ_k(σ) = tr(σ) = z`, and let each\n`χ_k(σ) = f_k·h/2 + c_k·[2]/2`. Then `Σ_k y_k c_k = (2z − h)/[2]`.\nThe inputs are the Markov normalisations, which hold for every `n`; so the\naverage does not depend on `n`. At `z = q³/(q²+1)` this is `(q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.eigen_trace_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.eigen_trace_split","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/DeterminantChern.lean#L80-L89","doc":"**The eigenvalue split of a Hecke generator's trace.** If `σ` acts with\neigenvalue `q` on an `m₊`-dimensional subspace and `−q⁻¹` on an\n`m₋`-dimensional one, its trace is `f·(q − q⁻¹)/2 + c₁·(q + q⁻¹)/2` with\n`f = m₊ + m₋` (the dimension) and `c₁ = m₊ − m₋` (the determinant exponent).\nThis is the crossing-energy split `E = ℓ·b + w·a`, with `ℓ ↔ f` and `w ↔ c₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.det_kronecker_inv_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.det_kronecker_inv_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/DeterminantChern.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**`c₁(Ad) = 0`.** The conjugation `X ↦ A X A⁻¹`, as the Kronecker matrix\n`A ⊗ (A⁻¹)ᵀ`, has determinant `1` for every invertible `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.det_evalWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.det_evalWord","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/DeterminantChern.lean#L54-L59","doc":"The determinant case: `det ρ(β) = det ρ(σ)^{w(β)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.character_evalWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.character_evalWord","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/DeterminantChern.lean#L38-L52","doc":"**An abelian character of a braid representation is `D ^ writhe`** when every\ngenerator has the same character value `D` (as for conjugate generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.evalWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.DeterminantChern.evalWord","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/DeterminantChern.lean#L34-L36","doc":"Evaluate a signed braid word with generator images `g`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}